id: pm-gh1484
title: "GH-1484: Infer native Node test telemetry and bound intentional test flush lifetime"
description: "GitHub #1484 reports that SDK package suites using node --test inherit NODE_TEST_CONTEXT=child-v8 without Vitest flags or NODE_ENV=test. Current inference omits that signal, so child CLI invocations can be recorded as ordinary activity. The report also describes an ENOTEMPTY cleanup race with a detached telemetry worker. Source inspection confirms the missing signal in consent and inline-flush selection; the reported cleanup race is not reproduced by this intake."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:sdk","area:telemetry",github-intake,test-isolation
created_at: "2026-10-16T09:35:02.376Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T09:37:06.080Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Native Node test children are inferred before identity creation, storage or export; explicit test-event consent and source-context overrides retain their documented behavior; intentional test delivery has a bounded worker lifetime and cleanup proof; ordinary production delivery and the existing deleted-root guard remain covered; Node and Bun package consumers have published-SDK regression evidence and updated configuration guidance."
definition_of_ready: "Read the current consent, source-context, Sentry and flush-worker policies and predecessor evidence. Choose a scoped native-test signal and intentional-delivery lifecycle policy, with isolated loopback and real child-process controls."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Classify native Node test children before telemetry identity or export and preserve a bounded lifecycle for intentionally enabled test delivery.
value: Keep operational context representative of real activity and make SDK package test cleanup reliable.
why_now: A new public SDK consumer report arrived during reviewed delivery; the supported package ecosystem uses native Node tests as well as Bun and Vitest.
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: "SDK-consuming package suites, native Node test children and disposable global trackers"
expected_result: Native Node tests receive consistent telemetry isolation; opted-in test delivery completes safely before disposable roots are removed.
actual_result: "Intake only: source policy and inline-flush selection recognize Vitest and NODE_ENV=test but omit NODE_TEST_CONTEXT. GitHub reports an SDK-package cleanup failure. No current fix or new cleanup reproduction is claimed."
affected_version: 2026.10.15
component: telemetry
